  "title": "Family",
  "description": "Learn words for family members and talk about the people closest to you.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to the Family unit! Talking about family introduces essential gender patterns in Portuguese. Most family nouns come in pairs: *o irmão* (the brother) and *a irmã* (the sister), or *o filho* (the son) and *a filha* (the daughter).\n\nPay special attention to accent marks when talking about grandparents! **O avô** (the grandfather) uses a circumflex accent (^) for a closed 'oh' sound, while **a avó** (the grandmother) uses an acute accent (´) for an open 'aw' sound.\n\nTo show possession, match the gender to the family member: use **meu** for masculine nouns (*meu pai*, *meu irmão*) and **minha** for feminine nouns (*minha mãe*, *minha irmã*).",
